#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK on various operating systems"
msgstr "Instalar el SDK de Qiskit en varios sistemas operativos"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install Qiskit"
msgstr "Instalar Qiskit"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore manylinux miniconda */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore manylinux miniconda */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit-install\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qiskit-install\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"
msgstr "Instalar Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whether you will work locally or in a cloud environment, the first step for all users is to install Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Ya sea que trabajes localmente o en un entorno en la nube, el primer paso para todos los usuarios es instalar Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"local\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"local\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK {#install-the-qiskit-sdk}"
msgstr "Instalar el SDK de Qiskit {#install-the-qiskit-sdk}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install Python. Check the \"Programming Language\" section on the [Qiskit PyPI project page](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) to determine which Python versions are supported by the most recent release. For download instructions, see the [Python Beginners Guide](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"
msgstr "Instala Python. Consulta la sección \"Programming Language\" en la [página del proyecto Qiskit en PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) para determinar qué versiones de Python son compatibles con la versión más reciente. Para instrucciones de descarga, consulta la [Guía para principiantes de Python](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    It is recommended that you use [Python virtual environments](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) to separate Qiskit from other applications.\n"
msgstr "    Se recomienda que utilices [entornos virtuales de Python](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) para separar Qiskit de otras aplicaciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    These instructions use the standard Python distribution from [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). However, you can use other Python distributions, such as [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) or [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), along with other dependency management workflows like [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    Estas instrucciones utilizan la distribución estándar de Python de [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). Sin embargo, puedes utilizar otras distribuciones de Python, como [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) o [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), junto con otros flujos de trabajo de gestión de dependencias como [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"If you're new to virtual environments, click to expand for more information.\">\n"
"    A virtual Python environment is an isolated space to work with Python for a specific purpose — so you can install whatever packages you wish, and set up libraries, dependencies, and so on, without affecting the \"base\" Python environment on your machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"Si eres nuevo en entornos virtuales, haz clic para ampliar y obtener más información.\">\n"
"    Un entorno virtual de Python es un espacio aislado para trabajar con Python para un propósito específico, de modo que puedes instalar los paquetes que desees y configurar bibliotecas, dependencias, etc., sin afectar el entorno Python \"base\" en tu máquina.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    One important advantage of a virtual environment is that if your Python environment becomes corrupted somewhere along the way, you can easily delete the virtual environment and start over!\n"
msgstr "    Una ventaja importante de un entorno virtual es que si tu entorno Python se corrompe en el camino, ¡puedes eliminar fácilmente el entorno virtual y comenzar de nuevo!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Choose a preferred location in which to store information about your virtual environments. Typically they're stored in a directory named `.venv` within each project directory you're working in.\n"
"    </AccordionItem>\n"
"    </Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"    Elige una ubicación preferida para almacenar información sobre tus entornos virtuales. Por lo general, se almacenan en un directorio llamado `.venv` dentro de cada directorio de proyecto en el que estés trabajando.\n"
"    </AccordionItem>\n"
"    </Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    First, navigate to your project directory and create a minimal environment with only Python installed in it.\n"
msgstr "    Primero, navega al directorio de tu proyecto y crea un entorno mínimo con solo Python instalado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Next, activate your new environment.\n"
msgstr "    A continuación, activa tu nuevo entorno.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
"              If using PowerShell:\n"
msgstr ""
"           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
"              Si utilizas PowerShell:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"             If using Git Bash:\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"             Si utilizas Git Bash:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             source .venv/scripts/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"              If using command prompt:\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             source .venv/scripts/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"              Si utilizas el símbolo del sistema:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Install pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) if it's not already installed in your environment. Pip is a Python package manager that you use to install Qiskit and other Python packages. Use `pip list` to see what is in your virtual environment. In most Python environments, pip is already installed.\n"
msgstr "[Instala pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) si aún no está instalado en tu entorno. Pip es un gestor de paquetes de Python que se utiliza para instalar Qiskit y otros paquetes de Python. Usa `pip list` para ver qué hay en tu entorno virtual. En la mayoría de los entornos de Python, pip ya está instalado.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK.\n"
msgstr "Instala el SDK de Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install qiskit\n"
"      ```\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install qiskit\n"
"      ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Add visualization support\">\n"
"      If you intend to use visualization functionality or Jupyter notebooks, also install the `qiskit.visualization` module. See the [Visualizations API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) for more information.\n"
"      </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"      <Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Agregar soporte de visualización\">\n"
"      Si tienes la intención de utilizar la funcionalidad de visualización o notebooks de Jupyter, instala también el módulo `qiskit.visualization`. Consulta la [referencia de la API de visualizaciones](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) para obtener más información.\n"
"      </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"local-jupyter\"></span>\n"
"1. If you want to run a Jupyter notebook with the Qiskit packages you just installed, you need to install Jupyter in your environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"local-jupyter\"></span>\n"
"1. Si deseas ejecutar un notebook de Jupyter con los paquetes de Qiskit que acabas de instalar, debes instalar Jupyter en tu entorno.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install jupyter\n"
"      ```\n"
"    Then open your notebook as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install jupyter\n"
"      ```\n"
"    Luego abre tu notebook de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      jupyter notebook <path/to/notebook.ipynb>\n"
"      ```\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      jupyter notebook <path/to/notebook.ipynb>\n"
"      ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are planning to work locally and use simulators built into Qiskit, then your installation is done. If you want to run jobs on IBM&reg; QPUs, continue on to [set up your IBM Cloud&reg; account](cloud-setup).\n"
msgstr "Si planeas trabajar localmente y utilizar simuladores integrados en Qiskit, entonces tu instalación está completa. Si deseas ejecutar trabajos en QPUs de IBM&reg;, continúa con [configurar tu cuenta de IBM Cloud&reg;](cloud-setup).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Stay current with the latest versions\">\n"
"Periodically check the [Qiskit release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes) to see new releases. We recommend frequently updating your requirements for `qiskit` by running `pip install -U qiskit`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mantente actualizado con las últimas versiones\">\n"
"Revisa periódicamente las [notas de versión de Qiskit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes) para ver las nuevas versiones. Recomendamos actualizar frecuentemente tus requisitos para `qiskit` ejecutando `pip install -U qiskit`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Solución de problemas {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`No Module 'qiskit'` error with Jupyter Notebook\">\n"
"  If you used ``pip install qiskit`` and set up your virtual environment in\n"
"  Anaconda, then you may get the ``No Module 'qiskit'`` error when you run a tutorial\n"
"  in Jupyter Notebook. If you have not installed Qiskit or set up your\n"
"  virtual environment, you can follow the [installation](#qiskit-install) steps.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Error `No Module 'qiskit'` con Jupyter Notebook\">\n"
"  Si utilizaste ``pip install qiskit`` y configuraste tu entorno virtual en Anaconda, es posible que obtengas el error ``No Module 'qiskit'`` cuando ejecutes un tutorial en Jupyter Notebook. Si no has instalado Qiskit o no has configurado tu entorno virtual, puedes seguir los [pasos de instalación](#qiskit-install).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The error is caused when trying to import the Qiskit package in an\n"
"  environment where Qiskit is not installed. If you launched Jupyter Notebook\n"
"  from the Anaconda-Navigator, it is possible that Jupyter Notebook is running\n"
"  in the base (root) environment, instead of in your virtual\n"
"  environment. Choose a virtual environment in the Anaconda-Navigator from the\n"
"  **Applications on** dropdown menu. In this menu, you can see\n"
"  all of the virtual environments within Anaconda, and you can\n"
"  select the environment where you have Qiskit installed to launch Jupyter\n"
"  Notebook.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"  El error se produce al intentar importar el paquete Qiskit en un entorno donde Qiskit no está instalado. Si iniciaste Jupyter Notebook desde Anaconda-Navigator, es posible que Jupyter Notebook se esté ejecutando en el entorno base (root), en lugar de en tu entorno virtual. Elige un entorno virtual en Anaconda-Navigator desde el menú desplegable **Applications on**. En este menú, puedes ver todos los entornos virtuales dentro de Anaconda y puedes seleccionar el entorno donde tienes Qiskit instalado para iniciar Jupyter Notebook.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Compilation errors during installation\">\n"
"  Qiskit depends on a number of other open-source Python packages, which\n"
"  are automatically installed when doing ``pip install qiskit``. Depending on\n"
"  your system's platform and Python version, it is possible that a particular\n"
"  package does not provide pre-built binaries for your system. You can refer\n"
"  to [Operating system support](#operating-system-support) for a list of platforms supported by Qiskit, some\n"
"  of which may need an extra compiler. In cases where there are\n"
"  no precompiled binaries available, ``pip`` will attempt to compile the package\n"
"  from source, which in turn might require some extra dependencies that need to\n"
"  be installed manually.\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Errores de compilación durante la instalación\">\n"
"  Qiskit depende de varios otros paquetes de Python de código abierto, que se instalan automáticamente al ejecutar ``pip install qiskit``. Dependiendo de la plataforma de tu sistema y la versión de Python, es posible que un paquete en particular no proporcione binarios precompilados para tu sistema. Puedes consultar [Soporte del sistema operativo](#operating-system-support) para obtener una lista de plataformas compatibles con Qiskit, algunas de las cuales pueden necesitar un compilador adicional. En casos donde no hay binarios precompilados disponibles, ``pip`` intentará compilar el paquete desde el código fuente, lo que a su vez puede requerir algunas dependencias adicionales que deben instalarse manualmente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If the output of ``pip install qiskit`` contains similar lines to:\n"
msgstr "  Si la salida de ``pip install qiskit`` contiene líneas similares a:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  please check the documentation of the package that failed to install (in the\n"
"  example code, ``SOME_PACKAGE``) for information on how to install the libraries\n"
"  needed for compiling from source.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  consulta la documentación del paquete que falló al instalar (en el código de ejemplo, ``SOME_PACKAGE``) para obtener información sobre cómo instalar las bibliotecas necesarias para compilar desde el código fuente.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"os-support\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"os-support\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operating system support {#operating-system-support}"
msgstr "Soporte del sistema operativo {#operating-system-support}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit strives to support as many operating systems as possible, but due to limitations in available testing resources and operating system availability, not all operating systems can be supported. Operating system support for Qiskit is broken into three tiers with different levels of support for each tier. For platforms outside these, such as FreeBSD or WebAssembly (WASI), Qiskit may still be installable, but it is not tested and you will have to build Qiskit (and likely Qiskit’s dependencies) from source.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit se esfuerza por admitir tantos sistemas operativos como sea posible, pero debido a limitaciones en los recursos de prueba disponibles y la disponibilidad del sistema operativo, no todos los sistemas operativos pueden ser compatibles. El soporte de sistemas operativos de Qiskit se divide en tres niveles, cada uno con un grado de soporte distinto. Para plataformas fuera de estas, como FreeBSD o WebAssembly (WASI), Qiskit aún puede ser instalable, pero no está probado y tendrás que compilar Qiskit (y probablemente las dependencias de Qiskit) desde el código fuente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additionally, Qiskit only supports the CPython implementation of the Python language. Running with other Python interpreters such as PyPy is not supported.\n"
msgstr "Además, Qiskit solo admite la implementación CPython del lenguaje Python. La ejecución con otros intérpretes de Python como PyPy no es compatible.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit v2.x {#qiskit-v2x}"
msgstr "Qiskit v2.x {#qiskit-v2x}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the Qiskit v2.x release series, the supported platforms are:\n"
msgstr "En la serie de versiones Qiskit v2.x, las plataformas compatibles son:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 1\">\n"
"  Tier 1 operating systems are fully tested as part of the development processes to ensure any proposed change will function correctly. Pre-compiled binaries are built, tested, and published to PyPI as part of the release process. Typically, as long as there is a functioning Python environment installed, Qiskit can be installed on these operating systems without needing to install further dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nivel 1\">\n"
"  Los sistemas operativos de nivel 1 se prueban completamente como parte de los procesos de desarrollo para garantizar que cualquier cambio propuesto funcione correctamente. Los binarios precompilados se construyen, prueban y publican en PyPI como parte del proceso de lanzamiento. Por lo general, siempre que haya un entorno de Python en funcionamiento instalado, Qiskit se puede instalar en estos sistemas operativos sin necesidad de instalar dependencias adicionales.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 1 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Sistemas operativos de nivel 1:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Linux x86_64 (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification).\n"
msgstr "Linux x86_64 (distribuciones compatibles con la especificación de empaquetado [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/)).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "macOS ARM64 (11.0 or newer)\n"
msgstr "macOS ARM64 (11.0 o más reciente)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Windows 64-bit (Windows 10 and later supported)\n"
msgstr "Windows 64-bit (Windows 10 y versiones posteriores compatibles)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - Linux AArch64 (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 2\">\n"
"  Tier 2 operating systems are not tested as part of the development process. However, pre-compiled binaries are built, tested, and published to PyPI as part of the release process, and these packages can be expected to be installed with only a functioning Python environment.\n"
"  There might be a delay in releasing packages for these systems, since test failures might not be detected until much later, and failures during publishing will not block the publication of the package for Tier 1 systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"  - Linux AArch64 (distribuciones compatibles con la especificación de empaquetado [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/))\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nivel 2\">\n"
"  Los sistemas operativos de nivel 2 no se prueban como parte del proceso de desarrollo. Sin embargo, los binarios precompilados se construyen, prueban y publican en PyPI como parte del proceso de lanzamiento, y se puede esperar que estos paquetes se instalen con solo un entorno de Python en funcionamiento.\n"
"  Puede haber un retraso en el lanzamiento de paquetes para estos sistemas, ya que las fallas en las pruebas pueden no detectarse hasta mucho más tarde, y las fallas durante la publicación no bloquearán la publicación del paquete para los sistemas de nivel 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 2 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Sistemas operativos de nivel 2:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - macOS x86_64 (10.12 or later)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 3\">\n"
"  Tier 3 operating systems are not tested as part of the development process. Pre-compiled binaries are built and published to PyPI as part of the release process but are not tested. They may not be installable with only a functioning Python environment and might require a C/C++ compiler or additional programs to build dependencies from source as part of the installation process. Support for these operating systems are best effort only.\n"
msgstr ""
"  - macOS x86_64 (10.12 o posterior)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nivel 3\">\n"
"  Los sistemas operativos de nivel 3 no se prueban como parte del proceso de desarrollo. Los binarios precompilados se construyen y publican en PyPI como parte del proceso de lanzamiento, pero no se prueban. Es posible que no sean instalables con solo un entorno de Python en funcionamiento y podrían requerir un compilador de C/C++ o programas adicionales para compilar dependencias desde el código fuente como parte del proceso de instalación. El soporte para estos sistemas operativos se ofrece solo en la medida de lo posible (sin garantías).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 3 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Sistemas operativos de nivel 3:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Linux ppc64le (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/)packaging specification)\n"
msgstr "Linux ppc64le (distribuciones compatibles con la especificación de empaquetado [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/))\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
